WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.150
A worker on a low income gets a pay rise.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.010
She now earns 100 pounds more.

3
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.570
Her employer pays every penny of it.

4
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.030
Nothing else about her job changes.

5
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.140
Yet when she works out what
she really has to spend,

6
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.380
she is only about 32 pounds better off.

7
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.650
So why can a pay rise leave a low-income

8
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.380
family barely any better off?

9
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.460
In this mission, you'll explore
the difference between an equal

10
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.410
share and a fair one.

11
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.120
Then you'll move a slider
and watch how a family's

12
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.710
income changes as its earnings grow.

13
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.280
Your mission: find out where
the rest of a pay rise goes.
